    "narrative": "The LawDog starting lineup for August 15th leans heavily into exploitable matchups against soft-tossing right-handers. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains our cornerstone anchor with a robust 67.97 score, while **Gleyber Torres** (67.52) and **Brendan Donovan** (66.36) offer the highest upside. **Gleyber Torres** benefits significantly from leading off against a sub-optimal lefty in Kay, while **Brendan Donovan** and **Cal Raleigh** (62.77) are positioned to feast on Hayden Wesneski\u2019s 4.92 xERA. Furthermore, **Jung Hoo Lee** (64.88) provides elite value; he is a primary target due to his 85% stolen base efficiency against a slower-delivery pitcher, combined with a favorable platoon advantage that pushes his efficiency well above his base projection.\n\nOur most critical decision at the margins involves **Lawrence Butler** (49.52), who remains in the lineup despite a difficult matchup against MacKenzie Gore. He narrowly edged out **Luis Arraez** (47.52) for the final UTIL spot; while **Luis Arraez** offers a higher floor for batting average, the optimizer favored **Lawrence Butler** due to park factors\u2014specifically the +10% boost in a favorable hitter's environment\u2014which outweighed the platoon penalty against the lefty. We are maintaining a cautious stance on **Masyn Winn** (52.55) due to a 37% rain risk in his contest against Matthew Boyd. Should the rain delay escalate, **JJ Bleday** is the primary contingency, though he carries his own weather risk (40%) that kept him off the active roster today. Keep a close watch on **Yainer Diaz**, who is currently slotted in the 9-hole; his 43.83 score is the lowest in the lineup, making him a candidate to be swapped if official lineups confirm a more detrimental batting order position.",
